@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### login as an Employee or Admin first (classify-ticket uses the same roles
### as ticket creation)

### classify a ticket before submitting it — works with no GROQ_API_KEY set
### (returns a heuristic "fallback" suggestion instead of an error).
### The answer includes "aiLogId": send it back when you create the ticket.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai-api/classify-ticket
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Wi-Fi keeps dropping on the 3rd floor",
  "description": "My laptop disconnects from CorpNet every few minutes since this morning. It's urgent, I can't join my calls."
}

### the same text again (within 24 h, key set) is answered from the earlier result, no model call

### create the ticket and tell the server which suggestion you saw.
### ticket.ai.acceptedByUser is computed by the server (category AND priority unchanged).
### Someone else's aiLogId, a junk id or a made-up "acceptedByUser" is ignored.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Wi-Fi keeps dropping on the 3rd floor",
  "description": "My laptop disconnects every few minutes",
  "categoryId": "PASTE_CATEGORY_ID",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "aiLogId": "PASTE_AI_LOG_ID"
}

### missing input -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai-api/classify-ticket
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### kb-suggestions — login as a Technician/Manager/Admin first
### (a plain Technician only gets suggestions for tickets in their own
### department, the same scope as GET /ticket-api/tickets/:id).
### Only PUBLISHED articles are ever suggested. With a key: AI-ranked (relevance, why, steps),
### saved on the ticket; without one or on failure: text order, source "retrieval".
GET {{baseUrl}}/ai-api/kb-suggestions/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID

### ask the model again instead of using the saved answer
GET {{baseUrl}}/ai-api/kb-suggestions/PASTE_TICKET_PUBLIC_ID?refresh=true

### an employee -> 403; a technician from another team -> 404
### per-user rate limit: more than AI_RATE_LIMIT_MAX (20) calls a minute -> 429
